:{"highlights":"; Highlights for TypeScript and JSX.\n;\n; When several patterns match a node, the last one wins, so general patterns\n; come first and more specific ones after them. Keywords come before names:\n; a contextual keyword used as a name (`x.type`, `{ get: 1 }`) is a name node\n; with the keyword token inside it, at the same position, and the name wins.\n\n; Punctuation\n; -----------\n\n[\n  \";\"\n  \".\"\n  \",\"\n  \":\"\n] @punctuation.delimiter\n\n(optional_chain) @punctuation.delimiter\n\n[\n  \"(\"\n  \")\"\n  \"[\"\n  \"]\"\n  \"{\"\n  \"}\"\n] @punctuation.bracket\n\n(type_arguments\n  [\n    \"<\"\n    \">\"\n  ] @punctuation.bracket)\n\n(type_parameters\n  [\n    \"<\"\n    \">\"\n  ] @punctuation.bracket)\n\n(template_substitution\n  [\n    \"${\"\n    \"}\"\n  ] @punctuation.special)\n\n(template_type\n  [\n    \"${\"\n    \"}\"\n  ] @punctuation.special)\n\n; Operators\n; ---------\n\n[\n  \"-\"\n  \"--\"\n  \"-=\"\n  \"+\"\n  \"++\"\n  \"+=\"\n  \"*\"\n  \"*=\"\n  \"**\"\n  \"**=\"\n  \"/=\"\n  \"%\"\n  \"%=\"\n  \"<\"\n  \"<=\"\n  \"<<\"\n  \"<<=\"\n  \"=\"\n  \"==\"\n  \"===\"\n  \"!\"\n  \"!=\"\n  \"!==\"\n  \"=>\"\n  \">\"\n  \">=\"\n  \">>\"\n  \">>=\"\n  \">>>\"\n  \">>>=\"\n  \"~\"\n  \"^\"\n  \"&\"\n  \"|\"\n  \"^=\"\n  \"&=\"\n  \"|=\"\n  \"&&\"\n  \"||\"\n  \"??\"\n  \"&&=\"\n  \"||=\"\n  \"??=\"\n  \"...\"\n  \"?\"\n  \"-?:\"\n  \"+?:\"\n  \"?:\"\n] @operator\n\n; `/` is also a regex delimiter.\n(binary_expression\n  operator: \"/\" @operator)\n\n(ternary_expression\n  [\n    \"?\"\n    \":\"\n  ] @keyword.conditional.ternary)\n\n(conditional_type\n  [\n    \"?\"\n    \":\"\n  ] @keyword.conditional.ternary)\n\n; Keywords\n; --------\n\n[\n  \"as\"\n  \"async\"\n  \"await\"\n  \"class\"\n  \"const\"\n  \"debugger\"\n  \"declare\"\n  \"delete\"\n  \"extends\"\n  \"get\"\n  \"implements\"\n  \"in\"\n  \"infer\"\n  \"instanceof\"\n  \"is\"\n  \"keyof\"\n  \"let\"\n  \"new\"\n  \"of\"\n  \"satisfies\"\n  \"set\"\n  \"typeof\"\n  \"